<section id="S5" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">V </span><span id="S5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Error Guarantee for MA-CDMP</span></h2>

<div id="S5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we focus on the theoretical guarantee for the convergence of the proposed MA-CDMP framework. Specifically, we first analyze the estimation error for the drift term of the diffusion SDE under MF approximation. Building on this, we provide an upper bound on the distributional error of conditional diffusion-based generation.</p>
</div>
<section id="S5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S5.SS1.6" class="ltx_text">V-A</span> </span><span id="S5.SS1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Theoretical Upper Bound on the Drift Term Approximation Error</span></h3>

<div id="S5.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Consistent with existing literature <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">30</a>]</cite>, we first make the following assumptions.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmassumption1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_assumption">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmassumption1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumption 1</span></span><span id="Thmassumption1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmassumption1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmassumption1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The classifier <math id="Thmassumption1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{J}_{\psi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{J}_{\psi}</annotation></semantics></math> and diffusion noise model <math id="Thmassumption1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\epsilon}_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\epsilon}_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> are L-smooth, with gradients that are Lipschitz-continuous with constants <math id="Thmassumption1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\mathcal{J}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\mathcal{J}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmassumption1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\bm{\epsilon}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\bm{\epsilon}}</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively:</p>
<table id="S5.E21" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S5.E21.1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E21.1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\parallel\!\nabla\!{\mathcal{J}}(\bm{x}^{(i)}\!,\!\bm{x}^{(j)})\!-\!\nabla\!{\mathcal{J}}(\bm{x}^{(i)}\!,\!\overline{\bm{x}}^{(i)})\!\parallel\leq L_{{\mathcal{J}}}\parallel\!\bm{x}^{(j)}\!-\!\overline{\bm{x}}^{(i)}\!\parallel," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mo>∥</mo></mpadded><mo>∇</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mpadded style="width:0.275em;" width="0.275em"><mo>,</mo></mpadded><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.052em" rspace="0.052em">−</mo><mo>∇</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mpadded style="width:0.275em;" width="0.275em"><mo>,</mo></mpadded><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mpadded style="width:0.219em;" width="0.219em"><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mpadded></mrow><mo rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0.0835em">≤</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi></msub><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo></mpadded><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.052em">−</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\parallel\!\nabla\!{\mathcal{J}}(\bm{x}^{(i)}\!,\!\bm{x}^{(j)})\!-\!\nabla\!{\mathcal{J}}(\bm{x}^{(i)}\!,\!\overline{\bm{x}}^{(i)})\!\parallel\leq L_{{\mathcal{J}}}\parallel\!\bm{x}^{(j)}\!-\!\overline{\bm{x}}^{(i)}\!\parallel,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21a)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S5.E21.2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E21.2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\parallel\nabla\bm{\epsilon}(\bm{x}^{(i)}\!,\!\bm{x}^{(j)})-\nabla\bm{\epsilon}(\bm{x}^{(i)}\!,\!\overline{\bm{x}}^{(i)})\!\parallel\leq L_{\bm{\epsilon}}\parallel\!\bm{x}^{(j)}\!-\!\overline{\bm{x}}^{(i)}\!\parallel." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mpadded style="width:0.275em;" width="0.275em"><mo>,</mo></mpadded><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mpadded style="width:0.275em;" width="0.275em"><mo>,</mo></mpadded><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mpadded style="width:0.219em;" width="0.219em"><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mpadded></mrow><mo rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0.0835em">≤</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi></msub><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo></mpadded><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.052em">−</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0.0835em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\parallel\nabla\bm{\epsilon}(\bm{x}^{(i)}\!,\!\bm{x}^{(j)})-\nabla\bm{\epsilon}(\bm{x}^{(i)}\!,\!\overline{\bm{x}}^{(i)})\!\parallel\leq L_{\bm{\epsilon}}\parallel\!\bm{x}^{(j)}\!-\!\overline{\bm{x}}^{(i)}\!\parallel.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21b)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmassumption2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_assumption">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmassumption2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumption 2</span></span><span id="Thmassumption2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmassumption2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmassumption2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The difference between observation trajectories is bounded as</p>
<table id="S5.E22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\bm{x}^{(j)}-\overline{\bm{x}}^{(i)}\|^{2}=\|\bm{x}^{(j)}\|^{2}+\|\overline{\bm{x}}^{(i)}\|^{2}-2(\bm{x}^{(j)})^{\top}\overline{\bm{x}}^{(i)}\leq C," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\bm{x}^{(j)}-\overline{\bm{x}}^{(i)}\|^{2}=\|\bm{x}^{(j)}\|^{2}+\|\overline{\bm{x}}^{(i)}\|^{2}-2(\bm{x}^{(j)})^{\top}\overline{\bm{x}}^{(i)}\leq C,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmassumption2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="Thmassumption2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> is a constant bound related to the magnitude of observation vectors.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 1</span></span><span id="Thmlemma1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Under Assumptions <a href="#Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 1. ‣ V-A Theoretical Upper Bound on the Drift Term Approximation Error ‣ V Error Guarantee for MA-CDMP ‣ Multi-Agent Conditional Diffusion Model with Mean Field Communication as Wireless Resource Allocation Planner" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> and <a href="#Thmassumption2" title="Assumption 2. ‣ V-A Theoretical Upper Bound on the Drift Term Approximation Error ‣ V Error Guarantee for MA-CDMP ‣ Multi-Agent Conditional Diffusion Model with Mean Field Communication as Wireless Resource Allocation Planner" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, for the MF communication mechanism, the drift term approximation error of the reverse-time SDE in Eq. (<a href="#S3.Ex2" title="In III-A2 Diffusion Models ‣ III-A Preliminaries ‣ III Preliminaries &amp; System Model ‣ Multi-Agent Conditional Diffusion Model with Mean Field Communication as Wireless Resource Allocation Planner" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>) admits an upper bound as</p>
<table id="S5.E23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{\text{drift}}\leq\frac{CL_{\bm{\epsilon}}\beta_{\tau}}{\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{\tau}}}+\sqrt{C}L_{\mathcal{J}}\beta_{\tau}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mtext>drift</mtext></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>τ</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>C</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{\text{drift}}\leq\frac{CL_{\bm{\epsilon}}\beta_{\tau}}{\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{\tau}}}+\sqrt{C}L_{\mathcal{J}}\beta_{\tau}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS1.8" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S5.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Based on the analysis in Appendix B of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib69" title="" class="ltx_ref">69</a>]</cite>, the MF approximation error admits an upper bound as</span></p>
<table id="S5.E24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E24.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\parallel{\mathcal{J}}(\bm{x}^{(i)},\overline{\bm{x}}^{(i)})-\mathcal{J}(\widetilde{\bm{x}}^{(i)})\parallel\leq CL_{{\mathcal{J}}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0.0835em">≤</mo><mi>C</mi><msub><mi>L</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\parallel{\mathcal{J}}(\bm{x}^{(i)},\overline{\bm{x}}^{(i)})-\mathcal{J}(\widetilde{\bm{x}}^{(i)})\parallel\leq CL_{{\mathcal{J}}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="S5.E25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E25.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\parallel\bm{\epsilon}(\bm{x}^{(i)},\overline{\bm{x}}^{(i)})-\bm{\epsilon}(\widetilde{\bm{x}}^{(i)})\parallel\leq CL_{{\bm{\epsilon}}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0.0835em">≤</mo><mi>C</mi><msub><mi>L</mi><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\parallel\bm{\epsilon}(\bm{x}^{(i)},\overline{\bm{x}}^{(i)})-\bm{\epsilon}(\widetilde{\bm{x}}^{(i)})\parallel\leq CL_{{\bm{\epsilon}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(25)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">Next, considering the gradient of the classifier over the observation trajectory, we have</span></p>
<table id="S5.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.Ex1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\parallel\nabla\!\mathcal{J}(\widetilde{\bm{x}}^{(i)})\!" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mo>∇</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\parallel\nabla\!\mathcal{J}(\widetilde{\bm{x}}^{(i)})\!</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle-\!\nabla\!\mathcal{J}(\bm{x}^{(i)}\!,\!\overline{\bm{x}}^{(i)})\parallel" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.052em">−</mo><mo>∇</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mpadded style="width:0.275em;" width="0.275em"><mo>,</mo></mpadded><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\!\nabla\!\mathcal{J}(\bm{x}^{(i)}\!,\!\overline{\bm{x}}^{(i)})\parallel</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\!\left\|\frac{1}{|\mathcal{N}_{i}|}\sum_{j\in\mathcal{N}_{i}}\big(\nabla\!{\mathcal{J}}(\bm{x}^{(i)}\!,\!\bm{x}^{(j)})\!-\!\nabla\!{\mathcal{J}}(\bm{x}^{(i)}\!,\!\overline{\bm{x}}^{(i)})\big)\right\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.108em">=</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>∇</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.052em" rspace="0.052em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>∇</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\!\left\|\frac{1}{|\mathcal{N}_{i}|}\sum_{j\in\mathcal{N}_{i}}\big(\nabla\!{\mathcal{J}}(\bm{x}^{(i)}\!,\!\bm{x}^{(j)})\!-\!\nabla\!{\mathcal{J}}(\bm{x}^{(i)}\!,\!\overline{\bm{x}}^{(i)})\big)\right\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\!\frac{1}{|\mathcal{N}_{i}|}\sum_{j\in\mathcal{N}_{i}}\parallel\nabla\!{\mathcal{J}}(\bm{x}^{(i)}\!,\!\bm{x}^{(j)})\!-\!\nabla\!{\mathcal{J}}(\bm{x}^{(i)}\!,\!\overline{\bm{x}}^{(i)})\parallel" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.108em">≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mo>∇</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mpadded style="width:0.275em;" width="0.275em"><mo>,</mo></mpadded><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.052em" rspace="0.052em">−</mo><mo>∇</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mpadded style="width:0.275em;" width="0.275em"><mo>,</mo></mpadded><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\!\frac{1}{|\mathcal{N}_{i}|}\sum_{j\in\mathcal{N}_{i}}\parallel\nabla\!{\mathcal{J}}(\bm{x}^{(i)}\!,\!\bm{x}^{(j)})\!-\!\nabla\!{\mathcal{J}}(\bm{x}^{(i)}\!,\!\overline{\bm{x}}^{(i)})\parallel</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.E26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.E26.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\!\frac{1}{|\mathcal{N}_{i}|}\sum_{j\in\mathcal{N}_{i}}L_{{\mathcal{J}}}\cdot\parallel\bm{x}^{(j)}-\overline{\bm{x}}^{(i)}\parallel," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.108em">≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mi>L</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\!\frac{1}{|\mathcal{N}_{i}|}\sum_{j\in\mathcal{N}_{i}}L_{{\mathcal{J}}}\cdot\parallel\bm{x}^{(j)}-\overline{\bm{x}}^{(i)}\parallel,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(26)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS1.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS1.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">where the third line follows from the triangle inequality, while the fourth line applies the Lipschitz-continuity condition in Eq. (<a href="#S5.E21.1" title="In 21 ‣ Assumption 1. ‣ V-A Theoretical Upper Bound on the Drift Term Approximation Error ‣ V Error Guarantee for MA-CDMP ‣ Multi-Agent Conditional Diffusion Model with Mean Field Communication as Wireless Resource Allocation Planner" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">21a</span></a>). With the bounded observation trajectory difference, this yields</span></p>
<table id="S5.E27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E27.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\parallel\nabla\!\mathcal{J}(\widetilde{\bm{x}}^{(i)})\!-\!\nabla\!\mathcal{J}(\bm{x}^{(i)},\overline{\bm{x}}^{(i)})\parallel\,\leq L_{\mathcal{J}}\sqrt{C}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mo>∇</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.052em" rspace="0.052em">−</mo><mo>∇</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.059em">∥</mo><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi></msub><msqrt><mi>C</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\parallel\nabla\!\mathcal{J}(\widetilde{\bm{x}}^{(i)})\!-\!\nabla\!\mathcal{J}(\bm{x}^{(i)},\overline{\bm{x}}^{(i)})\parallel\,\leq L_{\mathcal{J}}\sqrt{C}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(27)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS1.p2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS1.p2.4.1" class="ltx_text">Finally, combining Eq. (<a href="#S5.E25" title="In Proof. ‣ V-A Theoretical Upper Bound on the Drift Term Approximation Error ‣ V Error Guarantee for MA-CDMP ‣ Multi-Agent Conditional Diffusion Model with Mean Field Communication as Wireless Resource Allocation Planner" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">25</span></a>) and Eq. (<a href="#S5.E27" title="In Proof. ‣ V-A Theoretical Upper Bound on the Drift Term Approximation Error ‣ V Error Guarantee for MA-CDMP ‣ Multi-Agent Conditional Diffusion Model with Mean Field Communication as Wireless Resource Allocation Planner" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">27</span></a>), we have the lemma.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S5.SS2.6" class="ltx_text">V-B</span> </span><span id="S5.SS2.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Theoretical Upper Bound on the SDE-Based Generative Distribution Approximation Error</span></h3>

<div id="Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 1</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Under the MF communication mechanism, the conditional diffusion modeling error between the true initial distribution <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and the generated distribution after denoising <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> is upper bounded as</p>
<table id="S5.E28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E28.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="D_{\text{KL}}(p_{0}\|{q}_{0})\leq\frac{1}{2}M_{2}e^{-\bar{\beta}_{T}}+\frac{1}{2}\int_{0}^{T}\mathbb{E}\left[\tfrac{\delta_{\text{drift}}^{2}}{\beta_{\tau}}\right]\mathrm{d}\tau," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mtext>drift</mtext><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo>]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\text{KL}}(p_{0}\|{q}_{0})\leq\frac{1}{2}M_{2}e^{-\bar{\beta}_{T}}+\frac{1}{2}\int_{0}^{T}\mathbb{E}\left[\tfrac{\delta_{\text{drift}}^{2}}{\beta_{\tau}}\right]\mathrm{d}\tau,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(28)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where we denote <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{2}:=\mathbb{E}\left\|\bm{x}_{t}\right\|^{2}&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{2}:=\mathbb{E}\left\|\bm{x}_{t}\right\|^{2}&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math> as the second-order moment of the data along the SDE, and <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\beta}_{T}:=\int_{0}^{T}\beta_{\tau}\mathrm{d}{\tau}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>T</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\beta}_{T}:=\int_{0}^{T}\beta_{\tau}\mathrm{d}{\tau}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Before proving Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1. ‣ V-B Theoretical Upper Bound on the SDE-Based Generative Distribution Approximation Error ‣ V Error Guarantee for MA-CDMP ‣ Multi-Agent Conditional Diffusion Model with Mean Field Communication as Wireless Resource Allocation Planner" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, we introduce several key lemmas that establish the necessary theoretical groundwork.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 2</span></span><span id="Thmlemma2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Consider the Ornstein–Uhlenbeck (OU) process with time-varying coefficient in Eq. (<a href="#S3.E2" title="In III-A2 Diffusion Models ‣ III-A Preliminaries ‣ III Preliminaries &amp; System Model ‣ Multi-Agent Conditional Diffusion Model with Mean Field Communication as Wireless Resource Allocation Planner" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>). The KL divergence between <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{T}</annotation></semantics></math> and the standard Gaussian distribution <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies</p>
<table id="S5.E29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E29.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="D_{\text{KL}}(p_{T}\,\|\,\rho)\;\lesssim\;\tfrac{1}{2}M_{2}\cdot e^{-\bar{\beta}_{T}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≲</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\text{KL}}(p_{T}\,\|\,\rho)\;\lesssim\;\tfrac{1}{2}M_{2}\cdot e^{-\bar{\beta}_{T}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(29)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The proof of Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma2" title="Lemma 2. ‣ V-B Theoretical Upper Bound on the SDE-Based Generative Distribution Approximation Error ‣ V Error Guarantee for MA-CDMP ‣ Multi-Agent Conditional Diffusion Model with Mean Field Communication as Wireless Resource Allocation Planner" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> is provided in Appendix <a href="#A1" title="Appendix A Proof for Lemma ‣ Multi-Agent Conditional Diffusion Model with Mean Field Communication as Wireless Resource Allocation Planner" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A</span></a>. Notably, this estimate does not depend on the initial distance <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="D_{\text{KL}}(p_{0}\|\rho)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\text{KL}}(p_{0}\|\rho)</annotation></semantics></math>, as in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib54" title="" class="ltx_ref">54</a>]</cite>, and further extends the derivation in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib56" title="" class="ltx_ref">56</a>]</cite> to the time-varying OU process.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We define the relative Fisher information between <math id="S5.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\tau}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\tau}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{\tau}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\tau}</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="S5.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="J(p_{\tau}\,\|\,q_{\tau})=\int p_{\tau}(X_{\tau})\,\left\|\nabla\log\frac{p_{\tau}(X_{\tau})}{q_{\tau}(X_{\tau})}\right\|^{2}\,\mathrm{d}X_{\tau}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>J</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(p_{\tau}\,\|\,q_{\tau})=\int p_{\tau}(X_{\tau})\,\left\|\nabla\log\frac{p_{\tau}(X_{\tau})}{q_{\tau}(X_{\tau})}\right\|^{2}\,\mathrm{d}X_{\tau}</annotation></semantics></math>, and will have the following lemma.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 3</span></span><span id="Thmlemma3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Consider the following two Itô processes with the same diffusion term <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(\tau)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(\tau)</annotation></semantics></math></p>
<table id="S5.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.E30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.E30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{d}X_{\tau}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{d}X_{\tau}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.E30.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=F_{1}(X_{\tau})\,\mathrm{d}{\tau}+g({\tau})\,\mathrm{d}\bm{w}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒘</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=F_{1}(X_{\tau})\,\mathrm{d}{\tau}+g({\tau})\,\mathrm{d}\bm{w},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(30)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.E31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.E31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{d}Y_{\tau}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{d}Y_{\tau}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.E31.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=F_{2}(Y_{\tau})\,\mathrm{d}{\tau}+g({\tau})\,\mathrm{d}\bm{w}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒘</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=F_{2}(Y_{\tau})\,\mathrm{d}{\tau}+g({\tau})\,\mathrm{d}\bm{w},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(31)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmlemma3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{1}(X_{\tau}),F_{2}(Y_{\tau}),g({\tau})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{1}(X_{\tau}),F_{2}(Y_{\tau}),g({\tau})</annotation></semantics></math> are continuous functions. We assume the uniqueness and regularity condition:</p>
<ul id="S5.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S5.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S5.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The two SDEs have unique solutions.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S5.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S5.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{\tau},Y_{\tau}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{\tau},Y_{\tau}</annotation></semantics></math> admit densities <math id="S5.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\tau},q_{\tau}\in C^{2}(\mathbb{R}^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\tau},q_{\tau}\in C^{2}(\mathbb{R}^{d})</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S5.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T&gt;\tau&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T&gt;\tau&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="Thmlemma3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Then the evolution of <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="D_{\text{KL}}(p_{\tau}\,\|\,q_{\tau})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\text{KL}}(p_{\tau}\,\|\,q_{\tau})</annotation></semantics></math> is given by</p>
<table id="S5.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.Ex4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\partial}{\partial{\tau}}D_{\text{KL}}(" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\partial}{\partial{\tau}}D_{\text{KL}}(</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex4.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle p_{\tau}\,\|\,q_{\tau})=-\tfrac{1}{2}g({\tau})^{2}J(p_{\tau}\,\|\,q_{\tau})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>g</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p_{\tau}\,\|\,q_{\tau})=-\tfrac{1}{2}g({\tau})^{2}J(p_{\tau}\,\|\,q_{\tau})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.E32"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.E32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\mathbb{E}\!\left[\left\langle F_{1}(X_{\tau})-F_{2}(X_{\tau}),\nabla\log\frac{p_{\tau}(X_{\tau})}{q_{\tau}(X_{\tau})}\right\rangle\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\mathbb{E}\!\left[\left\langle F_{1}(X_{\tau})-F_{2}(X_{\tau}),\nabla\log\frac{p_{\tau}(X_{\tau})}{q_{\tau}(X_{\tau})}\right\rangle\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(32)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The proof of Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma3" title="Lemma 3. ‣ V-B Theoretical Upper Bound on the SDE-Based Generative Distribution Approximation Error ‣ V Error Guarantee for MA-CDMP ‣ Multi-Agent Conditional Diffusion Model with Mean Field Communication as Wireless Resource Allocation Planner" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> is included in Appendix <a href="#A2" title="Appendix B Proof for Lemma ‣ Multi-Agent Conditional Diffusion Model with Mean Field Communication as Wireless Resource Allocation Planner" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Now, we are ready to prove Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1. ‣ V-B Theoretical Upper Bound on the SDE-Based Generative Distribution Approximation Error ‣ V Error Guarantee for MA-CDMP ‣ Multi-Agent Conditional Diffusion Model with Mean Field Communication as Wireless Resource Allocation Planner" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.8" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S5.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">By applying the chain rule of KL divergence, the error can be decomposed as</span></p>
<table id="S5.E33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center">
<div id="S5.E33.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_markedasmath ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:225.1pt;height:8.800000000000001pt;vertical-align:-2.2pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-15.3pt,0.6pt) scale(0.9,0.9) ;">
<p id="S5.E33.2.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S5.E33.m1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="D_{\text{KL}}(p_{0}\|{q}_{0})\!\leq\!D_{\text{KL}}(p_{T}\|{q}_{T})\!+\!\mathbb{E}_{\bm{x}_{T}}D_{\text{KL}}\!\left(p(\bm{x}_{0}|\bm{x}_{T})\|q(\bm{x}_{0}|\bm{x}_{T})\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">≤</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.052em" rspace="0.052em">+</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\text{KL}}(p_{0}\|{q}_{0})\!\leq\!D_{\text{KL}}(p_{T}\|{q}_{T})\!+\!\mathbb{E}_{\bm{x}_{T}}D_{\text{KL}}\!\left(p(\bm{x}_{0}|\bm{x}_{T})\|q(\bm{x}_{0}|\bm{x}_{T})\right).</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</span></div></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="0" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(33)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">Since the reverse denoising process begins from Gaussian noise, i.e., <math id="S5.SS2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{T}\sim\mathcal{N}(\textbf{0},\bm{I})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">0</mtext><mo>,</mo><mi>𝑰</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{T}\sim\mathcal{N}(\textbf{0},\bm{I})</annotation></semantics></math>, the first term can be bounded by Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma2" title="Lemma 2. ‣ V-B Theoretical Upper Bound on the SDE-Based Generative Distribution Approximation Error ‣ V Error Guarantee for MA-CDMP ‣ Multi-Agent Conditional Diffusion Model with Mean Field Communication as Wireless Resource Allocation Planner" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>. For the second term in Eq. (<a href="#S5.E33" title="In Proof. ‣ V-B Theoretical Upper Bound on the SDE-Based Generative Distribution Approximation Error ‣ V Error Guarantee for MA-CDMP ‣ Multi-Agent Conditional Diffusion Model with Mean Field Communication as Wireless Resource Allocation Planner" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">33</span></a>), by applying Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma3" title="Lemma 3. ‣ V-B Theoretical Upper Bound on the SDE-Based Generative Distribution Approximation Error ‣ V Error Guarantee for MA-CDMP ‣ Multi-Agent Conditional Diffusion Model with Mean Field Communication as Wireless Resource Allocation Planner" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>
and the weighted Young inequality, we yield</span></p>
<table id="S5.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.Ex5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\partial}{\partial{\tau}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\partial}{\partial{\tau}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex5.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle D_{\text{KL}}\!\left(p_{\tau}\|q_{\tau}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle D_{\text{KL}}\!\left(p_{\tau}\|q_{\tau}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq-\tfrac{\beta_{\tau}}{2}J\!\left(p_{\tau}\|q_{\tau}\right)\!+\!\left(\tfrac{1}{2\beta_{\tau}}\mathbb{E}\!\left\|F_{1}\!-\!F_{2}\right\|^{2}\!+\!\tfrac{\beta_{\tau}}{2}J\!\left(p_{\tau}\|q_{\tau}\right)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">≤</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mpadded style="width:0.481em;" width="0.481em"><mi>J</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.052em" rspace="0.052em">+</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.052em">−</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo rspace="0.052em">+</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mpadded style="width:0.481em;" width="0.481em"><mi>J</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq-\tfrac{\beta_{\tau}}{2}J\!\left(p_{\tau}\|q_{\tau}\right)\!+\!\left(\tfrac{1}{2\beta_{\tau}}\mathbb{E}\!\left\|F_{1}\!-\!F_{2}\right\|^{2}\!+\!\tfrac{\beta_{\tau}}{2}J\!\left(p_{\tau}\|q_{\tau}\right)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.E34"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.E34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\tfrac{1}{2\beta_{\tau}}\mathbb{E}\!\left\|F_{1}-F_{2}\right\|^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\tfrac{1}{2\beta_{\tau}}\mathbb{E}\!\left\|F_{1}-F_{2}\right\|^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(34)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.p6.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p6.3.1" class="ltx_text">Integrating both sides of this inequality with respect to <math id="S5.SS2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> over the interval <math id="S5.SS2.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,T]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,T]</annotation></semantics></math> further yields</span></p>
<table id="S5.E35" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E35.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\bm{x}_{T}}D_{\text{KL}}\!\left(p(\bm{x}_{0}|\bm{x}_{T})\|q(\bm{x}_{0}|\bm{x}_{T})\right)\!\leq\!\textstyle\int_{0}^{T}\!\mathbb{E}\tfrac{1}{2\beta_{\tau}}\left\|\big(F_{1}\!-\!F_{2}\big)\right\|^{2}\!\mathrm{d}\tau." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mi>𝔼</mi><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.052em">−</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>d</mi><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\bm{x}_{T}}D_{\text{KL}}\!\left(p(\bm{x}_{0}|\bm{x}_{T})\|q(\bm{x}_{0}|\bm{x}_{T})\right)\!\leq\!\textstyle\int_{0}^{T}\!\mathbb{E}\tfrac{1}{2\beta_{\tau}}\left\|\big(F_{1}\!-\!F_{2}\big)\right\|^{2}\!\mathrm{d}\tau.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(35)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.p6.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p6.4.1" class="ltx_text">By substituting Eq. (<a href="#S5.E33" title="In Proof. ‣ V-B Theoretical Upper Bound on the SDE-Based Generative Distribution Approximation Error ‣ V Error Guarantee for MA-CDMP ‣ Multi-Agent Conditional Diffusion Model with Mean Field Communication as Wireless Resource Allocation Planner" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">33</span></a>) and incorporating the upper bound of the drift term error in Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 1. ‣ V-A Theoretical Upper Bound on the Drift Term Approximation Error ‣ V Error Guarantee for MA-CDMP ‣ Multi-Agent Conditional Diffusion Model with Mean Field Communication as Wireless Resource Allocation Planner" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, we obtain
the theorem.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmremarkx1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmremarkx1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Remark</span></span><span id="Thmremarkx1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmremarkx1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmremarkx1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1. ‣ V-B Theoretical Upper Bound on the SDE-Based Generative Distribution Approximation Error ‣ V Error Guarantee for MA-CDMP ‣ Multi-Agent Conditional Diffusion Model with Mean Field Communication as Wireless Resource Allocation Planner" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> establishes that the conditional diffusion modeling error of MA-CDMP under MF communication remains provably bounded. Different from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib54" title="" class="ltx_ref">54</a>]</cite>, which applies Girsanov’s theorem <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib55" title="" class="ltx_ref">55</a>]</cite> to bound the KL divergence, we employ a differential inequality argument that achieves the same conclusion without such restrictive assumptions. One significant advantage of our derivations is the contingency on a more relaxed and practical assumption: the approach in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib54" title="" class="ltx_ref">54</a>]</cite> requires Novikov’s condition, which may not always hold. Instead, our analysis depends on a trajectory-smoothness assumption only<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib56" title="" class="ltx_ref">56</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmremarkx1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmremarkx1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1. ‣ V-B Theoretical Upper Bound on the SDE-Based Generative Distribution Approximation Error ‣ V Error Guarantee for MA-CDMP ‣ Multi-Agent Conditional Diffusion Model with Mean Field Communication as Wireless Resource Allocation Planner" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> implies that with an appropriate noise schedule and well-trained model parameters, this bound ensures that the approximation error remains controlled, thereby guaranteeing the algorithm’s convergence and reliability in modeling the stochastic dynamics of multi-agent communication systems.</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S6" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">VI </span><span id="S6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Performance Evaluation</span></h2>

<div id="S6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we present numerical experiments to assess the performance and verify the effectiveness of the proposed MA-CDMP framework. We further examine key hyperparameters to characterize their influence and demonstrate robustness.</p>
</div>
<section id="S6.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S6.SS1.6" class="ltx_text">VI-A</span> </span><span id="S6.SS1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Experimental Settings</span></h3>

<div id="S6.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We implement the diffusion noise model <math id="S6.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\epsilon}_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\epsilon}_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> using a temporal U-Net<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib70" title="" class="ltx_ref">70</a>]</cite> with <math id="S6.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>8</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">8</annotation></semantics></math> residual blocks, organized into <math id="S6.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math> down-sampling layers and <math id="S6.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math> symmetric up-sampling layers. Timestep and condition embeddings are concatenated and injected into the first temporal convolution of each block. The classifier <math id="S6.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{J}_{\psi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{J}_{\psi}</annotation></semantics></math> adopts the down-sampling half of this U-Net, with a final linear layer to produce a scalar output. The inverse dynamics model <math id="S6.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\phi}</annotation></semantics></math> is designed as a feed-forward neural network that maps observation transitions to actions. To enhance efficiency and stability, parameters are shared among homogeneous agents.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We employ OPNET as the simulation platform of the wireless communication network. The simulated area spans <math id="S6.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>10</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10</annotation></semantics></math> km <math id="S6.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="S6.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>10</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10</annotation></semantics></math> km with communication nodes randomly distributed. Each node supports 1-hop transmission within a <math id="S6.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3.6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3.6</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3.6</annotation></semantics></math> km radius and operates over <math id="S6.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math> channels at a data rate of <math id="S6.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math> Mbps. Each transmission frame consists of <math id="S6.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>10</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10</annotation></semantics></math> time slots. To construct the offline dataset with diverse network loads, we configure scenarios with <math id="S6.SS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>8</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">8</annotation></semantics></math> nodes (high- to low-speed ratios of <math id="S6.SS1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2:6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2:6</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.SS1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4:4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4:4</annotation></semantics></math>) and <math id="S6.SS1.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>9</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">9</annotation></semantics></math> nodes (ratios of <math id="S6.SS1.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2:7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2:7</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.SS1.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4:5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4:5</annotation></semantics></math>). Packet generation follows an exponential distribution, with the mean arrival time adjusted based on the speed ratio and network topology to ensure load balancing and prevent congestion in dense regions. RBs are allocated according to the high- to low-speed ratio in each scenario. We record the environment data per frame, producing a dataset of <math id="S6.SS1.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1,000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1,000</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1,000</annotation></semantics></math> action-state trajectories labeled with rewards, each corresponding to a communication duration of <math id="S6.SS1.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="30" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>30</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">30</annotation></semantics></math> seconds (i.e., <math id="S6.SS1.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="6,000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>6,000</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">6,000</annotation></semantics></math> timesteps).</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">To assess the performance of the proposed MA-CDMP algorithm, we follow the evaluation in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib71" title="" class="ltx_ref">71</a>]</cite> and extend several state-of-the-art offline RL methods to the multi-agent setting under the DTDE paradigm. The compared baselines include MA-CQL<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib51" title="" class="ltx_ref">51</a>]</cite>, MA-TD3+BC<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib72" title="" class="ltx_ref">72</a>]</cite>, MA-Diffuser<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib38" title="" class="ltx_ref">38</a>]</cite>, MA-DT<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib73" title="" class="ltx_ref">73</a>]</cite>, and MA-DD<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">39</a>]</cite>. To further highlight the effectiveness of our framework, we also compare against MADiff <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib49" title="" class="ltx_ref">49</a>]</cite>, a representative algorithm under the CTDE scheme based on DMs. All methods are trained on the same offline dataset for <math id="S6.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="100" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>100</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">100</annotation></semantics></math> epochs, epoch comprising <math id="S6.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1{,}000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1,000</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1{,}000</annotation></semantics></math> training steps. During testing, the learned policies are deployed on the OPNET platform under random communication scenarios. Performance is measured over <math id="S6.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5</annotation></semantics></math>-second episodes using the average reward and key QoS metrics, including average throughput, average delay, and packet loss rate. We report the mean and standard deviation across <math id="S6.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math> independent scenario seeds to ensure statistical reliability. The key simulation parameters used throughout the experiments are listed in Table <a href="#S6.T2" title="TABLE II ‣ VI-A Experimental Settings ‣ VI Performance Evaluation ‣ Multi-Agent Conditional Diffusion Model with Mean Field Communication as Wireless Resource Allocation Planner" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">II</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S6.T2" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">TABLE II: </span>List of Key Parameter Settings for the Simulation.</figcaption>
<table id="S6.T2.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="S6.T2.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S6.T2.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_l ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:1pt;padding-bottom:1pt;">
<span id="S6.T2.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="S6.T2.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.T2.2.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Parameters Description</span></span>
</span></th>
<th id="S6.T2.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:1pt;padding-bottom:1pt;">
<span id="S6.T2.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:56.9pt;">
<span id="S6.T2.2.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.T2.2.1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Value</span></span>
</span></th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="S6.T2.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S6.T2.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_l ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:1pt;padding-bottom:1pt;">
<span id="S6.T2.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="S6.T2.2.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_p">Number of time slots in a frame</span>
</span></td>
<td id="S6.T2.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:1pt;padding-bottom:1pt;">
